<p>Contractors and regular customers can buy on account and pay later. Customers live in <strong>Customers</strong>; the till can
  add a new one too.</p>

<h2>Credit limits and terms</h2>
<p>Open the customer, press <strong>Edit</strong>, and give them a credit limit and payment terms (30 days is the default). A price list
  (contractor, wholesale) gives them their own prices whenever they're chosen at the till. A sale that would take them past their limit
  needs an owner's or manager's approval PIN.</p>

<h2>Selling on account</h2>
<p>At the till, choose the customer and pay <strong>On account</strong>. The sale is the invoice: it's due after their payment terms, and
  <strong>Tax invoice (A4)</strong> on the sale gives trade customers a proper tax invoice.</p>

<h2>Quotes and orders</h2>
<ol>
  <li>In <strong>Sell › Orders &amp; quotes</strong>, press <strong>New</strong>, choose the customer and add the goods. Save it as a quote,
    and send it as a PDF or by email. Quotes are valid for 14 days unless you change it.</li>
  <li>When the customer agrees, press <strong>Confirm order</strong>. <strong>Take deposit</strong> records money paid up front (cash,
    M-Pesa, card or bank).</li>
  <li>When the goods are in, press <strong>Mark ready to collect</strong> (with SMS on, the customer can be texted).</li>
  <li>When they come, press <strong>Collect at …</strong> on the order at the till: it's rung up at the quoted prices, with the deposit
    already counted.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Payments and statements</h2>
<p>Press <strong>Record payment</strong> on the customer to take money against their account; it settles their oldest sales first.
  <strong>Statement</strong> prints or emails what's owed and how old it is, and balance reminders can go by SMS. <strong>Customers › Who owes
  us</strong> lists every customer's balance by how late it is.</p>

<h2>Deliveries</h2>
<p>For goods going out on the lorry, press <strong>Deliver</strong> on the sale and print the delivery note with a signature line. Mark it dispatched with the driver
  and vehicle, then delivered with who received it and a photo of the signed note. <strong>Sell › Deliveries</strong> lists what's due out.</p>
